## Context
59 Write calls in the 14-day scan failed with "writes are limited to the worktree", and Read reports 17 "File does not exist" errors from cwd confusion (`docs/2026-10-21-velocity-friction-scan.md`). `rules/workflow.md` already says to use worktree-rooted paths; the agent still starts from the primary path in the transcript context.

Idea: the SessionStart hook prints the worktree root as a declarative line ("This session writes under <root>"), per `rules/claude-code.md` § Hook output. Estimate: 1 author-hour, about 50% chance of halving these errors. The root changes after the worktree is created, so check whether the hook can know it at start or must re-print after the `cd`.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Declarative root line present in session context after the worktree is entered
- [ ] Write-outside-worktree errors in a later window are below half of 59 per 14 days, or the shortfall explained

## Treatment
Treats: write_outside_worktree
Baseline: 2026-10-15=0 2026-10-16=0 2026-10-18=0 2026-10-19=0 2026-10-20=0 2026-10-21=0
